> ec [0,0,1,-1,0] on (0,0)
(0, 0) is on the curve (lhs - rhs = 0)
> ec [0,0,1,-1,0] on (0,-1)
(0, -1) is on the curve (lhs - rhs = 0)
> ec [0,0,1,-1,0] add (0,0) (1,0)
(0, 0) + (1, 0) = (-1, -1)
  check: the sum is on the curve
> ec [0,0,1,-1,0] add (0,0) (0,-1)
(0, 0) + (0, -1) = O
  check: the sum is on the curve
> ec [0,0,1,-1,0] mul 2 (0,0)
2 * (0, 0) = (1, 0)
> ec [0,0,1,-1,0] mul 7 (0,0)
7 * (0, 0) = (-5/9, 8/27)
> ec [0,0,1,-1,0] mul -5 (0,0)
-5 * (0, 0) = (1/4, -3/8)
> ec [0,0,1,-1,0] mul 0 (0,0)
0 * (0, 0) = O
> ec [0,0,1,-1,0] order (0,0)
(0, 0) has infinite order (no multiple up to 12 is O; Mazur: torsion orders are <= 12)
> ec [0,-1,1,-10,-20] add (5,5) (16,60)
(5, 5) + (16, 60) = (5, -6)
  check: the sum is on the curve
> ec y^2 = x^3 - x add (-1,0) (0,0)
(-1, 0) + (0, 0) = (1, 0)
  check: the sum is on the curve
> ec y^2 = x^3 - x + 1 mul 3 (-1,1)
3 * (-1, 1) = (1/4, 7/8)
> ec y^2 = x^3 - 2 mul 5 (3,5)
5 * (3, 5) = (307326105747363/160280942564521, 4559771683571581358275/2029190552145716973931)
> ec y^2 = x^3 - 26 add (3,1) (17/4,57/8)
(3, 1) + (17/4, 57/8) = (419/25, -8553/125)
  check: the sum is on the curve
> ec [0,0,1,-1,0] height (0,0)
canonical height of (0, 0): 0.051111408239969 (archimedean series error <= 5.1e-17)
  naive height log max(|num x|, |den x|): 0.000000000000000
